-- Source module: Solutions.KIL6NE
/-!
# KIL6: natural-number expressions

`NE` is a small language of natural-number expressions over registers (`+`, `-` (truncation
excluded by hypothesis), `*`, `/`, `%`, `if a < b then x else y`), compiled to `Ex HS`.
`NE.good`: on a state whose registers hold the naturals `v i`, if every intermediate value is
`≤ M` and `zsz M ≤ B`, then the compiled expression is clean, well defined, `B`-bounded and
evaluates to the natural value.  This turns every descriptor computation into arithmetic.
-/

